WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.363 --> 00:00:01.350
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.001
Today's message is
embrace your uniqueness.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:06.793
Over to you, Nina Dobrev.

00:00:06.793 --> 00:00:08.937
(rooster call)

00:00:08.937 --> 00:00:11.763
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.763 --> 00:00:14.532
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:18.439
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:21.544
- Honestly, I think everyone
is different and unique

00:00:21.544 --> 00:00:22.880
and that's a good thing.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:23.713
It's not bad.

00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:25.382
It's kind of the best thing in the world.

00:00:25.382 --> 00:00:27.367
You don't want to be like everyone else.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.189
Growing up in high school
and just junior high

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:32.322
just your whole life really,

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:33.155
either you have been taught to feel like,

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:36.155
or you want to be like everyone else

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.999
because conceptually you'll be included

00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:43.699
and you'll be like the crowd

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:45.944
but when you think about it,

00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:47.952
when you look at people like Lady Gaga

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:50.832
who is so crazy and so
different and so unique

00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:53.445
and her whole message is about, you know,

00:00:53.445 --> 00:00:55.670
being yourself and being okay with it.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.859
And she, the reason she
is so successful and so

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:01.395
is because she's talented,
because she's different.

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.160
If she was just like Britney Spears

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.696
of if she was just like me

00:01:05.696 --> 00:01:08.522
Nina Dobrev, then there would be two of us

00:01:08.522 --> 00:01:10.378
so there'd be nothing special about that.

00:01:10.378 --> 00:01:12.359
So I think what's special

00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:14.016
is the fact that you're different.

00:01:14.016 --> 00:01:15.391
And is the fact that you're unique

00:01:15.391 --> 00:01:16.979
and that you can bring
something to the table.

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.229
So if anything, embrace that uniqueness

00:01:21.709 --> 00:01:25.876
and that thing that you
have that no one else does

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:29.057
and expand upon it and make it better

00:01:29.057 --> 00:01:30.990
and tell everyone about it

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.123
and be confident in it.

00:01:32.123 --> 00:01:34.858
Because if you're confident
and happy and smiling

00:01:34.858 --> 00:01:38.711
you will attract confidence,
happiness and laughter.

00:01:38.711 --> 00:01:40.962
- People keep trying to copy
the successes of other people

00:01:40.962 --> 00:01:43.424
because they think it's
what's going to make them win

00:01:43.424 --> 00:01:45.619
and you can to some extent,

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:46.724
you can model success

00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:49.070
but if all you're doing
is copying somebody

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.157
step after step after step

00:01:51.157 --> 00:01:53.372
the best you're going to be

00:01:53.372 --> 00:01:55.070
is a second or third-rate version of them

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.191
Instead of the best version of you.

00:01:57.191 --> 00:01:58.917
And this is what's
really, really important.

00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:00.400
As you begin on your path,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.903
it's okay to copy other people.

00:02:01.903 --> 00:02:03.092
You're looking for guidance.

00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:04.053
You're looking for inspiration.

00:02:04.053 --> 00:02:05.649
You've no idea how anything is done.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:07.273
And so instead of trying to figure out

00:02:07.273 --> 00:02:08.527
every single idea yourself,

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.366
model success.

00:02:10.366 --> 00:02:11.787
Learn from the people
who've come before you.

00:02:11.787 --> 00:02:13.033
It's a fantastic strategy.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.861
But if you want to win the big game,

00:02:14.861 --> 00:02:16.253
if you want to really be unique

00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:17.401
and really different

00:02:17.401 --> 00:02:18.618
and really stand out

00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:19.950
and really have massive success,

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.759
it's going to come from you
taking these bits of pieces

00:02:21.759 --> 00:02:24.745
from other people, figure
what worked for them

00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:27.979
and then tweaking them to
apply to your situation.

00:02:27.979 --> 00:02:29.894
There's a great example I like
to reference on the channel

00:02:29.894 --> 00:02:31.426
talking about 50 Cent

00:02:31.426 --> 00:02:34.722
looking at new people coming
up through the industry

00:02:34.722 --> 00:02:36.166
and people sending him demo tapes

00:02:36.166 --> 00:02:38.278
and people that sound like Lil Wayne.

00:02:38.278 --> 00:02:39.568
He'll say, you sound just like Lil Wayne.

00:02:39.568 --> 00:02:41.750
I can't tell the difference
between you and Lil Wayne.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.925
It's amazing your talent to sound

00:02:42.925 --> 00:02:44.177
like Lil Wayne is fantastic

00:02:44.177 --> 00:02:46.838
but we already have a Lil Wayne.

00:02:46.838 --> 00:02:49.221
We don't need a Lil Wayne copycat.

00:02:49.221 --> 00:02:51.104
So the best you're going
to do here is just be

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.242
a Lil Wayne cover band.

00:02:53.242 --> 00:02:55.609
Is that what you want to do?

00:02:55.609 --> 00:02:57.356
Where you have uniqueness.

00:02:57.356 --> 00:02:58.560
You have talent inside you.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.109
You can find a way to tweak

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:01.580
some of the things that
worked for Lil Wayne

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.081
and apply it to your situation

00:03:03.081 --> 00:03:04.608
to be an amazing artist.

00:03:04.608 --> 00:03:06.932
I found this when I was
working on my YouTube channel

00:03:06.932 --> 00:03:08.600
and I was working with my agent.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.808
I had my agent, Steve

00:03:09.808 --> 00:03:11.187
and I had a media coach, Jenny

00:03:11.187 --> 00:03:12.746
who worked at the agency

00:03:12.746 --> 00:03:14.200
and they were giving me feedback

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.578
on how to make better videos.

00:03:15.578 --> 00:03:16.689
And I would meet with Jenny once a week

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:18.160
for a year and a half.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.584
And I met with Steve, maybe once a month

00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:20.731
looking at different videos.

00:03:20.731 --> 00:03:22.245
And they would always give me feedback

00:03:22.245 --> 00:03:23.544
and totally different style feedback.

00:03:23.544 --> 00:03:26.697
Steve was always, raise
the stakes, very aggressive

00:03:26.697 --> 00:03:28.540
why is this so important?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.366
What if somebody's
about to kill themselves

00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:31.617
before watching this video

00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:32.808
and you had to make that transition

00:03:32.808 --> 00:03:34.109
to help them stay alive, right.

00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:35.130
Just make it more important.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.512
And Jenny is leaning on authenticity.

00:03:37.512 --> 00:03:39.212
Understand and be genuine

00:03:39.212 --> 00:03:41.068
and a much softer side.

00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:42.678
And so every time I met with both of them,

00:03:42.678 --> 00:03:43.928
they would give me different feedback.

00:03:43.928 --> 00:03:46.793
And they see it through their lens

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.205
and I would always take their advice

00:03:49.205 --> 00:03:51.168
and I would struggle with it.

00:03:51.168 --> 00:03:52.594
And I would do exactly what they said.

00:03:52.594 --> 00:03:55.425
Steve gave me homework, I
would do exactly what he asked.

00:03:55.425 --> 00:03:57.465
Jenny gave me homework, I would
do exactly what she asked.

00:03:57.465 --> 00:03:59.138
And it always felt uncomfortable,

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:02.224
which was good, stretching
your comfort zone

00:04:02.224 --> 00:04:04.910
but it was never quite right for me.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.743
And what I had to do

00:04:05.743 --> 00:04:07.696
was take that awesome
piece of advice from Jenny

00:04:07.696 --> 00:04:09.480
and add just a little bit to it.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.632
Make it shift so that it worked for me.

00:04:12.632 --> 00:04:14.377
It felt more authentic.

00:04:14.377 --> 00:04:15.445
Felt more comfortable.

00:04:15.445 --> 00:04:16.572
Felt more Evan.

00:04:16.572 --> 00:04:17.873
And that's what you need to do.

00:04:17.873 --> 00:04:19.922
Look at all the strategies
of people that have gone out.

00:04:19.922 --> 00:04:21.059
What they've done before you,

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:21.956
it's amazing.

00:04:21.956 --> 00:04:23.348
And then see how can I make that thing

00:04:23.348 --> 00:04:24.568
that worked for Steve Jobs, work for me.

00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:26.667
What tweak can I make

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.928
to make it authentic and uniquely me

00:04:29.928 --> 00:04:32.771
so that I will have
success in this market?

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:33.670
Cause if you don't do that,

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.548
again you're just going to
be a copy of somebody else.

00:04:36.548 --> 00:04:38.030
And you're never going to stand out

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.236
and have massive success.

00:04:39.236 --> 00:04:42.347
You have amazingness inside you

00:04:42.347 --> 00:04:44.678
and you need to let that out.

00:04:44.678 --> 00:04:46.509
Trust that it's there.

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:48.085
Embrace it

00:04:48.085 --> 00:04:49.830
and go all in on it.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.743
So the question today is

00:04:50.743 --> 00:04:52.337
I'm curious what have you learned

00:04:52.337 --> 00:04:53.871
from somebody else that you've modeled

00:04:53.871 --> 00:04:55.608
and then tweaked.

00:04:55.608 --> 00:04:56.441
What was the tweak?

00:04:56.441 --> 00:04:57.274
I'm curious.

00:04:57.274 --> 00:04:58.107
What did you learn?

00:04:58.107 --> 00:04:58.940
And then how did you
tweak it to make it fit

00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.773
and work for you?

00:04:59.773 --> 00:05:01.386
Leave in the comments below.

00:05:01.386 --> 00:05:03.207
Super curious to find out.

00:05:03.207 --> 00:05:04.040
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Juliette Young.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.930
Juliette, thank you so much for picking up

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.197
a copy of my book Your One Word.

00:05:07.197 --> 00:05:09.142
It really, really,
really means a lot to me

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.666
and I appreciate the support.

00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:13.209
I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:05:13.209 --> 00:05:14.524
Thank you guys again for watching,

00:05:14.524 --> 00:05:15.497
I hope you have an amazing day.

00:05:15.497 --> 00:05:16.611
I believe in you

00:05:16.611 --> 00:05:18.645
and hope you continue
to believe in yourself

00:05:18.645 --> 00:05:20.181
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:20.181 --> 00:05:23.030
for another shot of entspresso.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.977
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:24.977 --> 00:05:28.394
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:31.718 --> 00:05:34.108
- Saying that we have enough artists,

00:05:34.108 --> 00:05:36.163
is like saying we have enough scientists.

00:05:36.163 --> 00:05:37.878
We have enough designers.

00:05:37.878 --> 00:05:39.487
We have enough politicians.

00:05:39.487 --> 00:05:40.533
We have enough politicians.

00:05:40.533 --> 00:05:41.974
(group laughter)

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:45.891
But you know, nobody gets
to be you except you.

00:05:47.785 --> 00:05:50.817
Nobody has your point of view except you.

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.610
Nobody gets to bring to the world

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:56.443
the things that you get
to bring to the world,

00:05:57.372 --> 00:06:00.446
uniquely get to bring
to the world except you.

00:06:00.446 --> 00:06:03.505
So saying there're
enough writers out there,

00:06:03.505 --> 00:06:04.760
enough directors out there,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.043
enough people with points of view.

00:06:06.043 --> 00:06:07.141
Well, yeah, there are but

00:06:07.141 --> 00:06:08.285
none of them are you.

00:06:08.285 --> 00:06:10.125
And none of those people

00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:11.858
is going to make the art you will make.

00:06:11.858 --> 00:06:14.254
None of them will change people

00:06:14.254 --> 00:06:15.149
and change the world

00:06:15.149 --> 00:06:17.406
in the way that you could change it.

00:06:17.406 --> 00:06:20.466
So if you believe somebody who says,

00:06:20.466 --> 00:06:22.770
no, no, we've got enough of those,

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:26.293
then all it means is you're
giving up your chance

00:06:26.293 --> 00:06:28.430
to change the world in the way that only

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.758
you could change it.

00:06:29.758 --> 00:06:31.673
- Everybody is the same and
I run into these people,

00:06:31.673 --> 00:06:35.585
I feel like nobody's a
real, real individual.

00:06:35.585 --> 00:06:38.324
It's rare that you stumble across someone

00:06:38.324 --> 00:06:39.451
who's a real individual and when you do

00:06:39.451 --> 00:06:40.487
it's like amazing.

00:06:40.487 --> 00:06:42.930
And I love seeing people who
are just truly themselves.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:46.237
But everybody's like
whatever they see on TV,

00:06:46.237 --> 00:06:47.199
whatever they see around them

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:48.277
they just want to be that.

00:06:48.277 --> 00:06:50.197
The world is huge, you
don't have to be that.

00:06:50.197 --> 00:06:52.745
You do not have to be
what your neighbor is.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.043
You don't have to do what
your neighbor is doing.

00:06:54.043 --> 00:06:55.573
You can do whatever the you want.

00:06:55.573 --> 00:06:57.091
So people are just like

00:06:57.091 --> 00:06:59.378
yeah, rappers feel like they
have to be a certain way.

00:06:59.378 --> 00:07:01.014
Actors feel like they
have to be a certain way.

00:07:01.014 --> 00:07:03.365
People in certain neighborhoods feel like

00:07:03.365 --> 00:07:04.229
they have to be a certain way

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:05.201
because who's there around.

00:07:05.201 --> 00:07:07.784
I know deep down like children,

00:07:08.805 --> 00:07:10.861
children are themselves,

00:07:10.861 --> 00:07:13.257
they react off of
instinct until they start

00:07:13.257 --> 00:07:14.509
to understand how the world is.

00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:17.759
In adults, once they turn into an adult

00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:21.805
they start to see, oh,
dang I can't do that,

00:07:21.805 --> 00:07:23.523
I can't like that no more.

00:07:23.523 --> 00:07:25.465
I can't be that way cause
that's not acceptable

00:07:25.465 --> 00:07:27.909
cause I might get looked down upon.

00:07:27.909 --> 00:07:29.824
They might laugh at me or think I'm weird.

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:30.867
And it's like, no, that.

00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:31.700
This is what makes you you.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.834
This is what makes you you.

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:35.635
Like I just try, it's hard to do,

00:07:35.635 --> 00:07:36.624
don't get me wrong.

00:07:36.624 --> 00:07:38.537
I'm still learning about myself.

00:07:38.537 --> 00:07:40.781
I'm trying to just open myself up

00:07:40.781 --> 00:07:43.669
to new ways of thinking all the time

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:44.955
and truly being myself.

00:07:44.955 --> 00:07:46.437
But sometimes I get caught in,

00:07:46.437 --> 00:07:48.089
so many different levels to a matrix,

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:49.377
you know what I'm saying.

00:07:49.377 --> 00:07:50.689
Sometimes, you're like
damn, I thought I was out

00:07:50.689 --> 00:07:51.604
and I was still in.

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.098
It's just,

00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:56.190
but yeah, it's just everybody
just feels like they have to

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.090
be just like everybody else.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:00.351
When I see rappers, I'm like come on dude.

00:08:00.351 --> 00:08:01.369
- They've got the same dance.

00:08:01.369 --> 00:08:02.202
- Same dance, dude.

00:08:02.202 --> 00:08:03.333
- The same turn up.

00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:04.570
- It's like dude, you
got a billion tattoos

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.873
on your face and body,
where did you get that from?

00:08:06.873 --> 00:08:09.749
Cause I know you didn't come
out of your mom's vagina

00:08:09.749 --> 00:08:11.461
going I want to be tatted.

00:08:11.461 --> 00:08:12.545
You saw somebody do that

00:08:12.545 --> 00:08:13.982
and you said I want to do that too

00:08:13.982 --> 00:08:15.898
cause that's going to make me look

00:08:15.898 --> 00:08:16.933
like this type of thing

00:08:16.933 --> 00:08:18.293
and I want to be just like that.

00:08:18.293 --> 00:08:19.372
And everybody's doing it,

00:08:19.372 --> 00:08:20.382
I know that works.

00:08:20.382 --> 00:08:21.325
So I'm going to do it

00:08:21.325 --> 00:08:22.869
and now it makes you look like one of them

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:24.201
and now you're not original

00:08:24.201 --> 00:08:25.638
and then when your rap
career doesn't go far,

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.230
you're like, what happened?

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:30.258
But it's not just rapping,
it's just all areas of life.

00:08:30.258 --> 00:08:31.833
- Staying power means hard work.

00:08:31.833 --> 00:08:34.925
Staying power means everyday you get up

00:08:34.925 --> 00:08:38.092
and you try to stay ahead of the pack.

00:08:39.993 --> 00:08:42.173
That sort of march to the
beat of your own drummer.

00:08:42.173 --> 00:08:46.210
This notion that music
becomes homogenized,

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.916
in other words, there are
lots of successful rappers

00:08:49.916 --> 00:08:52.047
but have short careers.

00:08:52.047 --> 00:08:55.107
Because if you can replace
one rapper for another,

00:08:55.107 --> 00:08:56.647
you're done.

00:08:56.647 --> 00:08:59.543
The more unique you are in what you do,

00:08:59.543 --> 00:09:02.356
the better your chances of continuing on.

00:09:02.356 --> 00:09:04.594
So when you take a look
at, sometimes it's musical,

00:09:04.594 --> 00:09:07.514
take a look at a band like AC/DC

00:09:07.514 --> 00:09:09.554
you hear it, you
immediately know what it is

00:09:09.554 --> 00:09:11.010
that's what they serve up.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.770
You want ballads, go to another band.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.238
They serve up, straight up.

00:09:14.238 --> 00:09:15.366
That's what you do.

00:09:15.366 --> 00:09:17.158
KISS serves up spectacle.

00:09:17.158 --> 00:09:21.486
We will not sit around on
stage on a Persian carpet,

00:09:21.486 --> 00:09:24.272
light candles and sing about,

00:09:24.272 --> 00:09:26.710
oh, the flaxen haired lass

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.030
and the English countryside.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.158
Kill me now.

00:09:30.158 --> 00:09:31.995
We don't do that.

00:09:31.995 --> 00:09:33.650
You know, you want nice quiet,

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:35.380
stay at home with grandma,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.678
pour another glass of water

00:09:36.678 --> 00:09:38.221
and put her false teeth in it.

00:09:38.221 --> 00:09:40.278
Let the spinach rise to the top.

00:09:40.278 --> 00:09:41.596
That ain't what we do.

00:09:41.596 --> 00:09:43.310
We blow stuff up.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.344
With a drummer and a backbeat.

00:09:46.344 --> 00:09:48.693
Don't sing about the secret of life

00:09:48.693 --> 00:09:50.208
cause there is none.

00:09:50.208 --> 00:09:51.639
Here's the secret of life,

00:09:51.639 --> 00:09:52.472
you're alive and then you're not.

00:09:52.472 --> 00:09:53.640
That's it.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.653
That's the secret.

00:09:55.653 --> 00:09:57.016
Be glad you're alive while you're alive,

00:09:57.016 --> 00:09:58.433
you're allowed to

00:09:59.869 --> 00:10:01.298
shake the world up a little bit

00:10:01.298 --> 00:10:02.136
and that's what you do.

